{
  "_comment": "Runner-jail seccomp profile (ADR 0050 / plan §9-D2). Default-deny (SCMP_ACT_ERRNO); only the syscalls a confined Node.js 22 runtime needs are allowed. Explicitly ABSENT (thus denied): ptrace, mount, umount2, keyctl, add_key, request_key, kexec_load, init_module, finit_module, bpf, setns, unshare, pivot_root, chroot, reboot. NOTE: basic clone() IS allowed (Node/libuv thread pool + worker_threads need it) but namespace-creating escapes are blocked by NOT allowing unshare/setns and by cap_drop ALL + no-new-privileges at the container layer (seccomp arg-filtering of clone flags is intentionally not attempted here). Validate: docker run --security-opt seccomp=./runner/seccomp-runner.json ... then run validate-jail.sh on the host.",
  "defaultAction": "SCMP_ACT_ERRNO",
  "architectures": [
    "SCMP_ARCH_X86_64",
    "SCMP_ARCH_X86",
    "SCMP_ARCH_X32"
  ],
